# Conventional-commit gate (Story #513).
#
# `rules/git-conventions.md` has always said this hook runs commitlint on
# every local commit; until #513 the hook did not exist, so nothing enforced
# the contract locally and a malformed subject was only ever caught — if at
# all — by the PR title that release-please parses.
#
# `--no-install` keeps the gate offline and deterministic: it fails loudly if
# commitlint is missing rather than silently fetching some other version.
npx --no-install commitlint --edit "$1"
